# Precision landing from our ArUco vision node (MAVLink LANDING_TARGET).
# Values tuned in SITL on the rough-sea scenario; see docs/SITL_GUIDE.md section 6 for the evidence.
PLND_ENABLED     1
PLND_TYPE        1
# 0 = raw measurements. The Kalman filter (1), with or without moving-target mode (PLND_OPTIONS 1),
# lags and overshoots a deck that sways every few seconds: rough-sea error ~1.9 m vs ~0.6 m raw.
PLND_EST_TYPE    0
PLND_OPTIONS     0
# If the target is lost, descend for PLND_TIMEOUT s, then climb and retry (up to RET_MAX times).
# 1 s rather than the default 4 s, so a retry can happen before the drone reaches the ground.
PLND_STRICT      1
PLND_RET_MAX     4
PLND_TIMEOUT     1
# Pause descent while further than this from the target. Tighter gating (0.3 m) made landings
# 4x slower and no more accurate.
PLND_XY_DIST_MAX 2.5
# Need a rangefinder (config/sitl_rangefinder.parm in SITL). Below ALT_MIN keep landing even if the
# pad leaves the camera view, which always happens in the last ~0.5 m. Above ALT_MAX the camera
# can't resolve the pad, so losing it is no reason to retry. Without a rangefinder set both to 0,
# otherwise ArduPilot treats a lost target as out of range and never retries.
PLND_ALT_MIN     0.5
PLND_ALT_MAX     10
# Vision pipeline latency (s). Measure on the real companion computer.
PLND_LAG         0.05
# Descent speeds, m/s (4.7 renamed LAND_SPEED/LAND_SPEED_HIGH, cm/s, to these).
# A faster final descent (0.7) was less accurate in rough sea.
LAND_SPD_MS      0.4
LAND_SPD_HIGH_MS 1.2
